WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.960
Sprout here! Today,

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.800
two scientists disagree.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:05.960
And I love that,

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.400
because there's a way to settle it.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:10.060
When two models compete,

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.660
you look for an observation where they predict different

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:14.120
things. That's the test.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:16.880
Model one says:

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:18.400
salt speeds up melting.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:19.720
Model two says:

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.740
salt changes nothing.

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:22.820
They disagree! So let's test it.

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:24.540
Two equal pieces of ice.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:26.260
Same room, same temperature.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:27.720
Salt on one.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.560
Model one predicts the salted ice melts first.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.200
Model two predicts a tie.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.160
If the salted ice melts first,

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:35.620
that supports model one.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.540
Make a small table.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.020
Each model, its prediction,

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:41.260
and what you observed.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:42.340
Then just compare.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.280
Your turn. Model A says heavier balls fall faster.

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.360
Model B says they fall at the same rate.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.120
You drop two balls together,

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.280
and they land together.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:53.560
Which model does that support?

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:54.940
Go.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:02.440
Model B! The observation matches its prediction.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:07.420
But careful. Agreement with one observation supports a model.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.080
It doesn't prove it's true everywhere,

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:09.980
forever.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:13.820
And when a question says according to model A,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.760
answer according to model A,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.680
even if another claim seems more familiar.

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.120
Now hit Try this skill!
